# Flowly – Privacy Policy

_Last updated: 17 October 2026_

Flowly is developed by Moritz Martin.
Contact: doublemlabs1@gmail.com

## Summary
Flowly works offline. Your financial data stays on your device and does not collect, store or share any personal data.

## Data stored on your device
Everything you enter in Flowly (transactions, categories, budgets, recurring entries, notes and receipt photos) is stored only on your device. Nobody else has access to it.

## Backups and exports
When you create a backup or a CSV export, the file is saved to the location you choose (for example your device storage or a cloud folder such as Google Drive). Once saved there, the file is handled by that storage provider under its own privacy policy. Flowly does not send these files anywhere else.

Your Flowly data is not included in Android's automatic cloud backup. If you transfer to a new phone with a direct device-to-device transfer, your data may be copied to the new device.

## App lock
If you enable the app lock, authentication (fingerprint, face or device PIN) is handled entirely by Android. Flowly never receives or stores biometric data.

## Purchases
Flowly Pro is purchased through Google Play. The payment is processed by Google under the [Google Privacy Policy](https://policies.google.com/privacy). Flowly only receives confirmation of whether Pro has been purchased. It receives no payment details.

## No tracking
Flowly contains no ads, no analytics, no tracking and no third-party SDKs that collect data.

## Your rights
Since Flowly does not process your personal data, there is nothing for Flowly to access, correct or delete. You can delete all your data at any time by uninstalling the app or clearing its storage. If you have questions, contact me at the email address above.

## Changes
If this policy changes, the updated version will be published on this page with a new date.
